@startuml MagicLinkSSO-Gate-Flow

title Magic Link SSO Gate Request Flow
hide footbox

participant "User's browser" as Browser
participant "Magic Link SSO Gate" as Gate
participant "SSO server" as SSO
participant "Private upstream\n(app or static site)" as Upstream

Browser -> Gate: Open protected page
Gate -> Gate: Validate own JWT cookie\nand check session revocation

alt Local session missing or invalid
    alt Browser SSO selected
        Gate --> Browser: Redirect to /_magicgate/sso/start\nwith original returnUrl
        Browser -> Gate: GET /_magicgate/sso/start
        Gate -> SSO: GET /sso/capabilities (backend)
        alt Browser SSO supported
            ref over Browser, SSO
                Browser SSO flow: hosted email/OTP or central reuse
                Application-owned forms: bootstrap flow
                Callback: /_magicgate/sso/callback
            end ref
        else auto mode: HTTP 404, disabled or unsupported
            ref over Browser, SSO: Email sign-in flow (browser SSO off)
        else Discovery failure or required support missing
            Gate --> Browser: Sign-in error; offer fresh start
        end
    else Browser SSO off
        ref over Browser, SSO
            Email sign-in flow (browser SSO off)
            Local UI: /_magicgate/login
            Hosted direct-use UI: SSO /signin
            Link callback: /_magicgate/verify-email
            Local OTP: POST /_magicgate/verify-email/otp
        end ref
    end

    opt Sign-in completed successfully
        Gate -> Gate: Validate returned JWT (iss, aud, signature)\nand set Gate-owned HttpOnly cookie
        note right of Gate
            Bootstrap sets this cookie before
            the issuer continuation; its finish
            callback retains the existing JWT.
        end note
        Gate --> Browser: Redirect to saved returnUrl
        Browser -> Gate: Request original protected page
        Gate -> Gate: Validate cookie and revocation
    end
end

opt Local session valid
    Gate -> Upstream: Proxy with forwarded identity headers
    Upstream --> Gate: HTML / assets / API / SSE / WebSocket handshake
    Gate --> Browser: Protected response
end

note over Gate, Upstream
Every protected request passes Gate's session check.
The upstream stays private and does not handle sign-in.
Auth and SSO transaction cookies are not forwarded upstream.
end note

== Sign Out ==

Browser -> Gate: POST /_magicgate/logout (same-origin)
Gate -> SSO: POST /logout (backend, current app JWT)
Gate --> Browser: Clear local cookie; public signed-out page\n(browser SSO mode enabled)
note over Browser, SSO
Central identity is retained. Ending browser SSO requires
the issuer's separate /sso/signout confirmation.
Gate paths include any configured namespace and public prefix.
end note

@enduml
